WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.430
Cole Hauser is known to many as tough guy
Rip Wheeler on Paramount's "Yellowstone."

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:08.530
He's the ranch foreman, who just so happens
to be the right-hand man to family patriarch

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:09.540
John Dutton.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:13.349
He's fiercely loyal both in terms of his work
on the ranch as well as his relationship with

00:00:13.349 --> 00:00:14.730
John's daughter, Beth.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:18.060
The two have maintained an intriguing yet
often heartwarming relationship throughout

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.300
the show's run, and it's only gotten more
intense going into Season 4.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.660
Beth's gone through a lot over the course
of the series.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:28.480
She survived a horrific attack against her
life, coming out of the situation relatively

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:29.480
unharmed.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:32.970
After escaping by the skin of her teeth, she's
continued to give back to her community, which

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:36.810
includes preventing a kid from falling into
homelessness, all while Rip has been there

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:37.930
by her side.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:40.220
That doesn't mean things have been easy for
the couple.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:43.550
They've gone through the wringer more than
a few times over the course of the show, and

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:47.100
luckily, the two actors have each other as
support when they're acting out emotional

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.100
scenes.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.220
According to Hauser, it's been an immense
pleasure working alongside someone as talented

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.134
as Kelly Reilly all these years.

00:00:53.134 --> 00:00:54.134
"What do you want?"

00:00:54.134 --> 00:00:56.140
"To make a scene.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:58.030
You ready to watch that happen?"

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:01.450
Even if you've only watched a couple of episodes
of "Yellowstone," you know it's an intense

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:02.450
show.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.860
It's undoubtedly hard work for the actors
once in a while to embody these characters,

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:08.120
so it helps when they get along with one another.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:12.090
That's the case with Hauser and Reilly, with
the former having nothing but praise for his

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.090
co-star.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:16.750
The actor sat down for an interview with CinemaBlend
to discuss acting alongside one of the finest

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:18.990
television actresses working today.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:19.990
As he put it,

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:23.990
"In Season 4, there's an obstacle or obstacles
that they have to face, and it was wonderful

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:25.250
doing it with Kelly.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:28.360
She's one of my favorite actresses I've ever
worked with, and working with her on this

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:30.140
relationship has just been so much fun."

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:33.840
Of course, it helps when the material is good
enough to stand on its own.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.780
In the same interview, Hauser praised the
show's creator, Taylor Sheridan, and the team

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:42.000
behind the scenes for crafting complex characters
who have continued to grow over the years,

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.000
saying,

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.850
"I mean, you know, once again, I think Taylor
[Sheridan] did just a fantastic job of putting

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:50.490
these two kids together, and seeing how they
can grow, and how their hearts can be more

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:51.490
open.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:55.400
How they can navigate different waters together,
and find even a stronger bond through those

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:56.400
waters."

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.450
Just like their characters, it's nothing but
love between these two.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:02.170
Hauser's not the only one who's enjoyed his
time with Reilly over the years.

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:06.270
Beth Dutton has a more tumultuous relationship
with her adopted brother, Jamie, played by

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:09.789
Wes Bentley, but Bentley still enjoys every
scene he gets to do with Reilly.

00:02:09.789 --> 00:02:12.400
In a similar interview with CinemaBlend, he
mentioned,

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.600
"[Kelly Reilly] is one of the sweetest people
and sweetest actors.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.370
She has to go so far to get to Beth.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.040
She does an amazing job."

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.560
Kelly Reilly may be intimidating as Beth,
but it's clear she knows how to turn on the

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.780
charm when the cameras stop rolling.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:27.810
It's good to hear that the two don't have
the same kind of relationship off of the set

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:29.040
that their characters have.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.900
It likely wouldn't result in the same kind
of dynamic because, as Bentley goes on to

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:36.819
state, there needs to be respect and admiration
toward your fellow actors to get a worthwhile

00:02:36.819 --> 00:02:40.450
performance, even if the characters are supposed
to hate one another.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:42.620
That's what Bentley goes on to mention in
the interview:

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:46.380
"It's hard because if you truly don't like
each other, it almost has the opposite effect.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:48.160
There's a lack of chemistry, you know?

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:51.180
You kind of have to have some connection to
really go for the anger."

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:55.709
And "anger" is definitely an apt word to describe
the relationship between Beth and Jamie.

00:02:55.709 --> 00:02:59.319
It's a good thing these actors all like each
other off-set because things are about to

00:02:59.319 --> 00:03:01.930
get messy over on the Dutton Ranch.

